      "title": "‘Exceedingly heavy-handed’: ACT police criticised by magistrate for Tasering disabled Aboriginal woman",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/10/exceedingly-heavy-handed-act-police-officers-criticised-by-magistrate-for-taser-arrest-of-disabled-aboriginal-woman-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive</strong>: Body-worn camera footage shows woman pulled off bench and a Taser activated despite ‘putting up no resistance’, magistrate says</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A magistrate has criticised “exceedingly heavy-handed” ACT police officers who Tasered an Aboriginal woman with an intellectual disability during a routine arrest.</p><p>The woman, named Emma, pleaded with officers not to use the stun gun on her and told them she was unarmed during the arrest at a Canberra bus stop in January.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/10/exceedingly-heavy-handed-act-police-officers-criticised-by-magistrate-for-taser-arrest-of-disabled-aboriginal-woman-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-09T14:00:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Settle down’ and ‘do your own swabs’: how alleged rape victims are treated in Queensland revealed in major report",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/10/settle-down-do-your-own-swabs-how-alleged-victims-are-treated-in-queensland-revealed-in-major-report",
      "description": "<p>Prosecutors dropped cases because survivors ‘didn’t act how a rape victim should’, Australian Institute of Criminology review of 19,000 sexual assault cases finds</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Queensland police put sexual assault investigations “on the backburner” because detectives were overworked and under pressure to prioritise cases linked to political issues such as youth crime, a major new study has found.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.aic.gov.au/sites/default/files/2026-11/crf_28_22-23_attrition_of_sexual_offences_in_police_investigations.pdf\">The report</a>, published this month by the Australian Institute of Criminology, sought to investigate why so many sexual assault complaints – about two-thirds of those made to police in Queensland – were withdrawn, not substantiated or considered unsolved.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/10/settle-down-do-your-own-swabs-how-alleged-victims-are-treated-in-queensland-revealed-in-major-report\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-09T14:00:12"
    },
    {
      "title": "There’s more than a whiff of politics to the sudden call to slash Labor’s green energy subsidies",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/10/labor-cuts-green-energy-subsidies-inflation",
      "description": "<p>EVs and home batteries are in Treasury’s crosshairs despite a better economic case for scaling back nuclear-powered submarines and diesel fuel rebates for miners</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>As Jim Chalmers, the treasurer, comes under increasing pressure to fight inflation by slashing spending in the midyear budget update, the drumbeat is loudest for cuts in one specific area: green energy subsidies for households.</p><p>Receiving the most focus is the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/ng-interactive/2026/may/31/cheaper-energy-bills-battery-revolution-climate-crisis\">cheaper home batteries program</a>, which from July last year has offered a taxpayer-backed 30% rebate to households and businesses.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/10/labor-cuts-green-energy-subsidies-inflation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-09T14:00:12"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stop undermining Jim Chalmers, environment minister urges Labor colleagues",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/09/stop-undermining-treasurer-jim-chalmers-environment-minister-urges-colleagues",
      "description": "<p>‘It’s pretty obvious that there are all sorts of people making all sorts of comments,’ Murray Watt says after budget savings meeting</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/mar/17/australia-environment-murray-watt-ocean-protection-fishers-drillers\">environment minister, Murray Watt</a>, has urged ministers to stop undermining the treasurer, Jim Chalmers, as Labor struggles to sell its budget and looks to cut popular clean energy subsidies to help with the fight against inflation.</p><p>Cabinet ministers met again on Monday to discuss potential budget savings to be included in next month’s mid-year update, part of efforts to reducing spending to ease pressure on the economy.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/09/stop-undermining-treasurer-jim-chalmers-environment-minister-urges-colleagues\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
